    "traits": "Acid, Invocation",
    "description": "<p><strong>ACID INVOCATION SAVE</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tradition</strong> arcane, verdant; <strong>Cast</strong> 2 AP (somatic, verbal); <strong>Saving Throw</strong> Fortitude; <strong>Base Damage</strong> 1d6; <strong>Duration</strong> 1 minute</p>\n<p>Upon completing the casting of this spell, your hands are infused with acidic energy. Your unarmed strikes inflict 1d6 secondary acid damage. Additionally, a successful melee attack causes the target to make a Fortitude save.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is Sickened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Fumble</strong> The target is Sickened 2.</p>\n<p><em>Automated:</em> for 1 minute your unarmed Strikes deal 1d6 secondary acid damage, and every melee Strike you hit with makes the target save Fortitude against your spell save DC (B8-2): Success or Partial unaffected, Failure Sickened 1, Fumble or Blunder Sickened 2. Sickened stays until it is removed. Nothing is rolled when you cast it.</p>"
